  "term": "multiple-task performance",
  "definition": "Multiple-task performance is a person’s ability to coordinate and carry out several tasks at the same time, especially when they must be monitored under tight deadlines. In this source, it is treated as a form of multitasking linked to executive functioning across adulthood, with spatial ability also contributing in some groups.",
